    "---\n",
    "## Task 3: Threshold Analysis\n",
    "A logistic regression model predicts P(Fraud). Results at threshold=0.5: TP=80, FP=20, FN=30, TN=870.\n",
    "\n",
    "**a)** Calculate Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1 Score.  \n",
    "**b)** For a bank minimising financial fraud loss, which metric should be maximised?  \n",
    "**c)** If we lower threshold to 0.3: TP=100, FP=50. Recalculate Precision and Recall.  \n",
    "**d)** Which threshold is better for the bank? Justify."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "task3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Task 3: Threshold Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_metrics(TP, FP, FN, TN, label=\"\"):\n",
    "    total = TP + FP + FN + TN\n",
    "    accuracy  = (TP + TN) / total\n",
    "    precision = TP / (TP + FP)\n",
    "    recall    = TP / (TP + FN)\n",
    "    f1        = 2 * (precision * recall) / (precision + recall)\n",
    "    print(f\"--- {label} ---\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Accuracy  : {accuracy*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Precision : {precision*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Recall    : {recall*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  F1 Score  : {f1*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "    return accuracy, precision, recall, f1\n",
    "\n",
    "# a) Metrics at threshold=0.5\n",
    "print(\"a) Metrics at threshold = 0.5:\")\n",
    "TP, FP, FN, TN = 80, 20, 30, 870\n",
    "acc05, prec05, rec05, f105 = compute_metrics(TP, FP, FN, TN, \"Threshold = 0.5\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# b) Which metric matters most\n",
    "print(\"\\nb) For a bank minimising fraud loss:\")\n",
    "print(\"   -> Prioritise RECALL\")\n",
    "print(\"   Reason: Each missed fraud (FN) = direct financial loss.\")\n",
    "print(\"   A false alarm (FP) just triggers an investigation -- less costly than missing real fraud.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# c) Metrics at threshold=0.3\n",
    "print(\"\\nc) Metrics at threshold = 0.3 (TP=100, FP=50, FN=10, TN=840):\")\n",
    "# FN = original 30 - 20 caught more = 10, TN = 870 - 50 new FPs = 820... recalculate correctly\n",
    "# Original positives = TP+FN = 80+30 = 110. New TP=100, so FN=10.\n",
    "# Original negatives = FP+TN = 20+870 = 890. New FP=50, so TN=840.\n",
    "TP2, FP2, FN2, TN2 = 100, 50, 10, 840\n",
    "_, prec03, rec03, _ = compute_metrics(TP2, FP2, FN2, TN2, \"Threshold = 0.3\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# d) Which threshold is better\n",
    "print(\"\\nd) Which threshold is better for the bank?\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Threshold 0.5 -> Recall = {rec05*100:.1f}%, Precision = {prec05*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Threshold 0.3 -> Recall = {rec03*100:.1f}%, Precision = {prec03*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(\"   -> Threshold 0.3 is better for the bank.\")\n",
    "print(\"   Higher Recall catches more real fraud cases (fewer missed transactions).\")\n",
    "print(\"   The cost of false alarms (extra reviews) is lower than missed fraud losses.\")"
   ]
